WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.441 --> 00:00:04.630
Unit eleven. Password Security Best Practices!

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.696
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.746 --> 00:00:13.061
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.111 --> 00:00:17.799
Today we learn about Password Security Best Practices. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.578 --> 00:00:24.311
Password security. Say it with me. Password security!

6
00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:32.608
Strong password. Say it with me. Strong password!

7
00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:40.631
Unique password. Say it with me. Unique password!

8
00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:48.680
Password manager. Say it with me. Password manager!

9
00:00:52.095 --> 00:00:57.191
Two-factor authentication. Say it with me. Two-factor authentication!

10
00:01:00.737 --> 00:01:05.237
Avoid reuse. Say it with me. Avoid reuse!

11
00:01:08.713 --> 00:01:12.462
Complexity. Say it with me. Complexity!

12
00:01:16.014 --> 00:01:20.531
Account protection. Say it with me. Account protection!

13
00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:35.293
Password security best practices include a strong, unique password for each account. A password manager and two-factor authentication add extra account protection.

14
00:01:35.343 --> 00:01:39.054
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:39.784 --> 00:01:45.111
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:45.161 --> 00:01:46.760
Unique password!

17
00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:53.234
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:53.284 --> 00:01:54.487
Complexity!

19
00:01:55.603 --> 00:02:03.744
Did you know? If a single website with your reused password is hacked, criminals can try that same password on many other accounts too!

20
00:02:03.794 --> 00:02:05.941
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:07.264 --> 00:02:17.237
Think and answer. Why is it risky to reuse the exact same password across multiple accounts?

22
00:02:17.287 --> 00:02:18.437
Great answer!

23
00:02:19.491 --> 00:02:25.138
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:25.188 --> 00:02:28.463
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

